1
00:00:00,380 --> 00:00:04,220
What if your worst haircut became your best escape plan?

2
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:06,160
This is Oh No My Hair,

3
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:09,820
a two-player cooperative puzzle platformer by NPC Union.

4
00:00:11,170 --> 00:00:14,950
Imagine two friends visit a salon at closing time.

5
00:00:15,130 --> 00:00:17,870
The barber just leaves his robot assistant in charge.

6
00:00:18,470 --> 00:00:20,870
Then the scissors suddenly go wrong,

7
00:00:20,930 --> 00:00:25,550
their hair gains unexpected powers, and the front door just locks.

8
00:00:25,550 --> 00:00:28,870
That means you have to escape from the house,

9
00:00:29,050 --> 00:00:32,870
and moreover, escaping means learning to trust each other.

10
00:00:34,390 --> 00:00:36,430
Twin-Tails can glide, pull levers,

11
00:00:36,450 --> 00:00:38,270
and carry her partner through the air.

12
00:00:38,610 --> 00:00:41,690
She creates routes and keeps her friend above danger.

13
00:00:41,950 --> 00:00:44,270
Her movement ability becomes a shared resource,

14
00:00:44,270 --> 00:00:46,690
rather than just a personal advantage.

15
00:00:48,063 --> 00:00:51,023
Pompadour can dash through gel, parry flying scissors,

16
00:00:51,303 --> 00:00:53,143
and launch a teammate from his head.

17
00:00:54,143 --> 00:00:55,663
His tools complement hers.

18
00:00:56,263 --> 00:00:57,963
One player opens a route;

19
00:00:57,963 --> 00:01:00,043
the other makes that route usable for both.

20
00:01:01,363 --> 00:01:03,683
Our signature moment is the sling dash.

21
00:01:03,683 --> 00:01:07,003
Twin-Tails carries Pompadour over the pit.

22
00:01:07,703 --> 00:01:10,803
He launches out of her grip, punches through a

23
00:01:10,803 --> 00:01:14,083
regrowing gel curtain, and she follows before it closes.

24
00:01:14,603 --> 00:01:17,063
The solution belongs to both players.

25
00:01:18,257 --> 00:01:21,457
Cooperation also changes what a projectile can do.

26
00:01:21,757 --> 00:01:23,217
Pompadour parries a scissor.

27
00:01:23,217 --> 00:01:26,317
Twin-Tails catches it with her hair and tosses

28
00:01:26,317 --> 00:01:29,197
it upward to ring a service bell.

29
00:01:29,197 --> 00:01:32,697
An enemy attack becomes the key to the next door.

30
00:01:34,047 --> 00:01:36,267
The salon is part of the puzzle, also.

31
00:01:36,587 --> 00:01:40,947
Water makes hair heavy and temporarily disables key abilities.

32
00:01:41,507 --> 00:01:43,787
Hair dryers, however, just restore those

33
00:01:43,787 --> 00:01:46,307
powers and create rising air currents.

34
00:01:46,627 --> 00:01:48,847
That means familiar tools ask players

35
00:01:48,847 --> 00:01:51,507
to rethink their timing and their route.

36
00:01:52,677 --> 00:01:55,417
The finale combines aimed scissors,

37
00:01:55,417 --> 00:01:59,977
overhead warnings, charging attacks, showers, and roaming robots.

38
00:02:00,477 --> 00:02:03,477
Players create a counterattack window and strike together.

39
00:02:03,477 --> 00:02:06,197
Hair swaps can also exchange their roles,

40
00:02:06,197 --> 00:02:09,697
turning a familiar partnership into an unexpected challenge.

41
00:02:10,997 --> 00:02:13,897
Better Together is our rule for level design.

42
00:02:13,897 --> 00:02:16,317
Carry me. Wait for the water.

43
00:02:16,377 --> 00:02:17,197
Parry now.

44
00:02:17,597 --> 00:02:20,737
A bad haircut becomes a warm story about trust.

45
00:02:22,053 --> 00:02:24,073
Our audience is friends, siblings,

46
00:02:24,093 --> 00:02:28,013
and couples who enjoy cooperative puzzles and playful platforming.

47
00:02:28,173 --> 00:02:29,693
One shared keyboard and a browser

48
00:02:29,693 --> 00:02:32,683
make the prototype easy to try together.

49
00:02:33,890 --> 00:02:36,210
PICO PARK 2 serves larger cooperative groups.

50
00:02:36,210 --> 00:02:39,510
Ibb and Obb explores two-player gravity puzzles.

51
00:02:39,890 --> 00:02:43,970
Our niche, on the other hand, is two asymmetric hair abilities,

52
00:02:44,110 --> 00:02:46,790
combination moves, and a compact salon escape.

53
00:02:46,790 --> 00:02:48,970
We still need to validate the demand.

54
00:02:50,403 --> 00:02:53,223
The prototype has 4 chapters, 12 rooms,

55
00:02:53,303 --> 00:02:57,643
a 3-phase boss, story sequences, saved progression and room replay.

56
00:02:57,643 --> 00:03:01,963
It is now publicly playable on itch.io.

57
00:03:02,313 --> 00:03:05,943
Future expansion will depend on testing with more pairs.

58
00:03:07,147 --> 00:03:10,567
Our indicative budgets are 20,000 US dollars for

59
00:03:10,567 --> 00:03:14,647
a 12-week minimum version, 60,000 for 24 weeks,

60
00:03:14,727 --> 00:03:19,307
or 120,000 for an expanded 36-week scope.

61
00:03:19,787 --> 00:03:22,307
These are planning estimates, not funding raised.

62
00:03:23,633 --> 00:03:28,633
The minimum allocates 12,000 to development, 3,000 to art and audio,

63
00:03:28,693 --> 00:03:32,373
1,000 to testing and tools, and 4,000 to contingency.

64
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:34,700
Weeks 1 to 4:

65
00:03:34,700 --> 00:03:37,060
playtests and onboarding. Weeks 5 to 8:

66
00:03:37,060 --> 00:03:39,920
polish rooms, controls, and visual feedback.

67
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:40,920
Weeks 9 to 12:

68
00:03:40,920 --> 00:03:44,840
accessibility checks, bug fixing, and release preparation.

69
00:03:45,260 --> 00:03:47,880
Expansion follows player evidence.

70
00:03:49,500 --> 00:03:51,560
Next, we plan to test 20 player pairs,

71
00:03:51,560 --> 00:03:55,600
tracking unaided tutorial completion, repeated failure points,

72
00:03:55,600 --> 00:03:57,540
and willingness to play another room.

73
00:03:58,120 --> 00:04:01,800
These are future validation targets, not achieved audience metrics.

74
00:04:03,043 --> 00:04:04,560
We are NPC Union:

75
00:04:04,560 --> 00:04:06,513
ChenHongshan333 and ZSYUYIIE.

76
00:04:06,513 --> 00:04:08,313
We are seeking playtest feedback and

77
00:04:08,313 --> 00:04:11,473
incubation support to polish this cooperative experience.

78
00:04:12,717 --> 00:04:15,107
So, at the end, scan the code to

79
00:04:15,107 --> 00:04:16,807
play and tell us what you think.

80
00:04:16,807 --> 00:04:18,427
Oh No My Hair.

81
00:04:18,607 --> 00:04:20,087
Bad hair, good friends.

82
00:04:20,367 --> 00:04:21,327
Thank you for listening.
